==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|ballista||a military siege engine for throwing stones|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bəˈlɪst.ɪk/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|not comparable}} Or relating to [[ballistics]].
# {{context|comparable}} Or relating to [[projectile]]s moving under their own [[momentum]], air drag, [[gravity]] and sometimes [[rocket]] power
# {{context|comparable|slang}} Very [[angry]].
#: ''When he heard him lie about it, he went '''ballistic'''.''

====Synonyms====
